{#
    Sidebar nav renderer. Three macros:
      - nav_item(item, current_route)            renders one <li><a></a></li>
      - nav_group(group, current_route)          renders one group, with a heading
                                                  (if group.label) and its visible items
      - icon_d(name)                             returns the Heroicons `d=` string
                                                  for a given icon key

    The icon map is local to `icon_d` because macros in Twig do not
    inherit top-level `{% set %}` variables from the file they're defined
    in — they only see their arguments and their own locals. Owning the
    map in a macro keeps it private and avoids polluting the calling
    template's scope.

    Icons are Heroicons 24/outline single-path SVGs, all with
    stroke-linecap/linejoin=round. To add an icon: append a key to
    `icon_d`'s map with the path's `d=` attribute, then reference it
    by name from `_sidebar.html.twig`'s `nav_groups` config.

    Graceful collapse: `nav_group` calls `nav_item_is_visible` on each
    item and renders nothing (no <h2>, no rule) if no items remain for
    the current user. A ROLE_USER with no MANAGE_* permissions sees no
    "Administration" group at all.
#}

{# @var item array {
        label:        string,
        route:        string,   route name (for path())
        route_prefix: string,   used for active-state matching via `starts with`
        permission:   string|null,   App\Security\Permission::* constant name (without prefix)
        icon:         string,   key passed to icon_d()
    }
   @var current_route string #}
{% macro nav_item_is_visible(item) -%}
    {%- if item.permission is null -%}
        1
    {%- elseif is_granted(constant('App\\Security\\Permission::' ~ item.permission)) -%}
        1
    {%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}

